{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>I will not destroy it if I find there</b> — He promises him that He will not destroy if such a number is found there. And He did not say to him, 'Know that there are not there the number you have spoken,' because their judgment was not yet completed, as He said, 'I will go down now and see' (Genesis 18:21). Now, Abraham did not know what would be done to them, and therefore he rose early in the morning and looked out toward the face of Sodom, and when he saw that they were destroyed, he knew that there were not that many there."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:21:17.012340964Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}